// dna/core/face.hl — a named face (Phase 3 DNA item 6, named faces).
//
// A face is a role an application fills: a door to the organism. An
// organism names one by a param of its main locus, of this type, built by
// the literal and recognised by the type, as `std::observe::Probes` is:
//
//   admin: dna::Face = dna::Face { app: "faces/admin", roles: "operator", consumes: "Orders", port: 8801 };
//
// The param's name is the face's. `app` is the seed of the application
// (static files with a generated client, or an application that serves a
// surface of its own), `roles` the roles it acts under and `consumes` the
// surfaces of the program it calls (each a space-separated list of names, as
// `std::api::StaticRoles.known` is), and `port` the loopback port `hale
// dna dev` and `run` serve it on. The type carries no behaviour: the
// compiler reads the literal into the description (`hale check --api`),
// the record's graph holds the face as a seed that consumes those
// contracts, and the standard face lists it in its navigation.
type Face {
    app: String = "";
    roles: String = "";
    consumes: String = "";
    port: Int = 0;
}
